  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main a6bd69d8).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe STEP importer's facet budget (the constant `MAX_FACETS`) becomes a setting that travels with the import (`app::geometry::import::step_budget`):\n\n- **Default and bounds.** The default is today's cap, 30,000,000 facets, so no default import changes and no golden moves. A set budget must be in 1,000..=60,000,000. Outside that range, every door refuses it by name before parsing (`STEP facet budget N is outside 1000..=60000000 facets`). A budget given for an STL or OBJ file is also refused.\n- **Doors.**\n  - `ImportModel::within(path, budget)` is the one command the GUI, the script and MCP all build.\n  - The script verb is `cam.import(path, name?, facetBudget?)`. A null name keeps the file stem. `cam.d.ts` is regenerated to match.\n  - MCP `import_model` takes an optional integer `facet_budget`, declared in the schema with its min/max.\n  - Script and MCP take whole numbers only. A fraction, a negative or a string is refused, never rounded.\n- **Recorded with the model.**\n  - A new component, `schema::StepBudget`, holds the budget, but only when it is not the default. `model_fidelity::budget_of` / `set_budget` read and write it.\n  - Import, update (re-import), repair (keeps it), delete and their undo all trade it together with the facets.\n  - The project file stores it as an optional `facet_budget` key. An absent key means the default, so default documents save byte for byte as before and older files load unchanged. An out-of-bounds value, or one on a non-model row, is refused by name at load.\n  - `get_job` and `cam.import` report the budget.\n- **Reduced fidelity (#864) is computed exactly as before.** A smaller budget flags the model; a larger one meshes finer and clears the flag on re-import. The refusal text now names a setting that exists: \"re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\".\n- **GUI.** The model page has a \"STEP facet budget (next import)\" row (type a value, then Enter or Set). An out-of-range value is refused by name on the row and on the status line, and the last good value stays. The row also shows which budget the model was imported under. Every STEP import started from the window (Model button, recent list, drag and drop) reads the setting. A re-import under the same name stays the undoable `UpdateModel`.\n- **`step.rs` edits are minimal.** `parse_with_chord_budget` was added, and the thread-local test override now only lowers the requested budget. This should merge additively with #969's log-line change.\n\nDecisions (60M ceiling, a session-scoped GUI setting on the model page rather than a post-picker modal, re-import uses the current setting, no project version bump) are in `docs/decisions/1054-step-facet-budget.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/step_budget.rs` (new, 6 tests):\n  - `the_default_budget_imports_exactly_as_before`\n  - `a_lowered_budget_flags_and_a_raised_one_clears_through_undo_and_delete`\n  - `an_out_of_bounds_budget_is_refused_by_name_before_parsing`\n  - `the_script_verb_takes_the_budget_and_refuses_one_out_of_bounds`\n  - `mcp_import_model_takes_the_budget_and_get_job_reports_it`\n  - `the_budget_round_trips_through_the_project_and_an_older_file_reads_the_default`\n- `step_budget::tests` unit tests: bounds, JSON whole numbers only, the default records nothing.\n- `crates/ui` `egui_app::tests::step_budget::the_model_page_sets_the_budget_the_next_step_import_runs_under`: the row is drawn, an out-of-range value is refused on the row and the status line, a lowered budget's import lands flagged, a raised re-import clears the flag, and undo restores both.\n- `crates/app/tests/model_fidelity.rs`: the two refusal-text pins now expect the new wording.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green on c93c64ef (app suites ok 167 s, ui suites ok 21 s, 3.1 min wall, 0 failed)\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real model that needs more than the 30M default to reach full fidelity. No such fixture is committed. \"Raised clears\" is pinned from 2,000 up to 5,000,000 on `Milling-test.step`.\n- The native file picker and typing into the egui field by keyboard. The test drives the setter and the import queue.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill doc does not mention `facet_budget` yet. It is a process file, which would need a `PROCESS_VERSION` bump; the tool's schema and description carry the argument.\n\nChangelog: The STEP facet budget is a setting: the model page, `cam.import(path, name?, facetBudget?)` and MCP `import_model`'s `facet_budget` set it (1000..=60000000, default 30000000), and each model records the budget it was imported under (#1054)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1054\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
